I like to spice up my Nethack game, but I'm not brave enough to try
conducts, so I settled upon a themed ascension, if you will.  The
conditions for Makoto Shishio were as follows:
A) Use Fire Brand
B) Wear a mummy wrapping
And, C) Be chaotic

B was somewhat annoying in that I had to keep my amulet of reflection
on instead of life saving (something that had cost me a Monk a couple
games prior,) but C was the big sticking point.  Being a Chaotic
Samurai isn't as fun as it might sound on its face; for one, you still
lose alignment for using poisoned weapons or attacking innocents.
And, of course, there was the problem of becoming Chaotic in the first
place.  Fortunately, I happened upon a cursed scroll of genocide.  I
summoned a group of white unicorns in a Chaotic temple, and the deed
was done relatively painlessly.

Set in my new direction, I set about to sacrificing for Fire Brand;
I'd been reluctant to do so earlier because I didn't want weapons I
couldn't use.  The first corpse I plunked down on the altar, a blade
materialized at my waiting feet...

Orcrist.  Gee, you shouldn't have.

I used all of my scrolls and wands of create monster before recalling
that I had seen a sink and an altar on the same level.  I spent around
10,000 turns pudding farming, and Susanowo emptied the garage on me -
Werebane, Stormbringer (although I did get some use out of that one,)
Trollsbane, Ogresmasher, Dragonbane, -Sting-... finally Susanowo
coughed up Frost Brand, and I felt I was getting somewhere.  Indeed, a
few dozen black pudding corpses later, I had my Fire Brand and
Susanowo had the fixings for an incredible Jell-O party (yes, I'm
aware that black pudding is actually a kind of sausage.)

Anyway, cleaning up the mess took another thousand turns or so; some
black puddings had even gotten through the Quest portal.  (Curiously,
my Quest leader didn't say anything about my conversion.)

Other than that, not much of note happened, besides smoky potions
being full healing, and me getting quite a few wishes while raising my
maximum HP.  Unable to think of anything else, I asked for magic
markers, and in fact I ended up running out of blank paper before I
did marker ink.  Funny, yes, but it was more painful at the time.
Speaking of pain, this was my first game in a while where I'd had to
take on Gehennom without a spell of magic mapping.  That wasn't too
fun either.

Amazingly, the mysterious force did nothing to me as I was escaping
Gehennom.  Maybe going Chaotic hadn't been such a waste after all.
The endgame was fairly run-of-the-mill.  I did use confused taming on
Air to gain around 10 pets, all of whom promptly died on Fire, as my
pets are wont to do.  I found the Neutral altar first, then Lawful,
then finally slogged my way to Chaotic.

